-- title:
--   Containment O ⊆ W for an end of the blow-up
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$ and a nonzero natural number $M'$ with $q \nmid M'$, together with a prime $\ell$ satisfying $\ell \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ and $\ell \mid M'$. Let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero and $\zeta \in L$ a primitive $q$-th root of unity, and assume (`hι`) that there is a ring homomorphism $\iota : L \to \mathbb{C}$ with $\iota(\zeta) = \exp(2\pi i/q)$. Let $H_1 \le (\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times$ be, by `hH₁`, the intersection of [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH q M'`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelJacobian.html#L22) — the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/q)^\times$, i.e. the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q$ — with the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/\ell)^\times$. Let $K$ be an intermediate field of $L \subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ which, by `hK`, is [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.xHFunctionField (q^2*M') H₁)`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103): the field generated over $L$ inside $L((t))$ by the coefficientwise image under [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81) of the rational $q$-expansion function field of level $\Gamma_{H_1}(q^2M')$.
--
--   Let $A$ be a Henselian discrete valuation domain with $L$ as fraction field and algebraically closed residue field, with $q \in \mathfrak{m}_A$ (`hAq`) and with $\zeta$ in the image of $A$ (`hζA`), and let $K$ be an $A$-algebra compatibly with $L$. Let $j \in K$ be an element, nonzero, whose Laurent expansion is the image under [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81) of [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157) (`hj`). Let $\varpi$ generate $\mathfrak{m}_A$ (`hϖ`) and let $\varpi_t \in A$ satisfy $\varpi_t^{\,q^2-1} = q\,u$ for a unit $u$ (`hϖt`). Write $C :=$ `chartAlgFin A ↥K j`, the $A$-subalgebra of elements of $K$ integral over $A[j]$, and `jChartFin` for $j$ viewed in $C$. Let $y$ be a maximal ideal of $C$ (`hy`) containing the image of $\varpi$ (`hϖy`) which is supersingular in the sense of `hss`: for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi : C \to \Omega$ with kernel $y$, the value $\varphi(j)$ lies in [`ModularCurve.ssJSet q Ω`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularModuli.html#L7), the set of those $\jmath \in \Omega$ such that every elliptic curve over $\Omega$ with $j$-invariant $\jmath$ has no nonzero point killed by $q$.
--
--   Throughout, for $\gamma \in SL(2,\mathbb{Z})$ an automorphism $\tau$ of $K$ over $L$ is called a level automorphism at $\gamma^{-1}$ when [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.IsLevelAutAt L q ζ q (q^2*M') H₁ γ⁻¹ K τ`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelLevelAutAt.html#L29) holds, that is: for all weights $k$, all modular forms $f,g$ of weight $k$ for $\Gamma_{H_1}(q^2M')$ with integral $q$-expansions $p_f,p_g$ and $p_g \neq 0$ in $L((t))$, and every $x \in K$ whose Laurent expansion is the image of $p_f/p_g$, the image of the expansion of $\tau x$ under any embedding $\iota : L \to \mathbb{C}$ normalising $\zeta$ to $\exp(2\pi i/q)$, multiplied by the $q$-expansion of $g \mid_k \mathrm{conjElemN}\,q\,\gamma^{-1}$, equals the $q$-expansion of $f \mid_k \mathrm{conjElemN}\,q\,\gamma^{-1}$.
--
--   The hypothesis `hArig` is a rigidity package for the two-chart integral model $X :=$ [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A ↥K j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236) (the pushout gluing $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the $j$-chart and the $j^{-1}$-chart over the middle chart). It asserts: for every point $z$ of $X$ at which the germ $\varpi_z$ of $\varpi$ (pulled back from $\operatorname{Spec} A$ along `toBase`) lies in the maximal ideal of the stalk, and every point $y'$ of `XFin A ↥K j` mapping to $z$ under `ιFin` whose prime ideal satisfies the same supersingularity condition as in `hss`, there exist a complete discrete valuation domain $W$, a ring homomorphism $\sigma : A \to W$ with $\mathfrak{m}_W = (\sigma\varpi)$, power series $f,u,v \in W[[X_0,X_1]]$ with $u,v$ units and $f \equiv X_0X_1^q - X_0^qX_1$ modulo $(X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$ (the Drinfeld form [`DrinfeldCurve.LocalChart.drinfeldForm q W`](def/DrinfeldCurve_LocalChart.html#L18)), and a ring isomorphism $e$ from the adic completion of the stalk $\mathcal{O}_{X,z}$ onto $S := W[[X_0,X_1]]/(C(\sigma(\varpi_t^{q+1}))v - fu)$, such that seven clauses hold (summarised here, with `toC` the map to the completion, `mkS` the quotient map onto $S$ and `germY` the germ map $C \to \mathcal{O}_{X,z}$ through the chart): (i) $e$ carries the germ of $a \in A$ to the class of $C(\sigma a)$; (ii) every level automorphism $\tau$ at $\gamma^{-1}$ with $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ maps $C$ into $C$; (iii) if moreover $\gamma_{11} \equiv 1 \pmod \ell$, the induced endomorphism of $C$ is the identity modulo the prime of $y'$; (iv) for $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ and such a $\tau$ which is the identity on $C$ modulo $y'$, there are a ring automorphism $\theta$ of $S$, an element $c \in W$ and a matrix $M \in M_2(W)$ with $\theta$ intertwining $e \circ \mathrm{toC} \circ \mathrm{germY}$ with the action of $\tau$ on $C$, $\theta$ fixing all constants $C(w)$, $\theta(X_{jj}) \equiv \sum_{ii} C(M_{ii\,jj})X_{ii}$ modulo the square of the ideal generated by the classes of $X_0,X_1$, $c^{q+1} \equiv 1$ and $M_{ii\,jj} \equiv c\,\gamma_{ii\,jj}$ modulo $\mathfrak{m}_W$, $c \equiv 1 \pmod{\mathfrak{m}_W}$ whenever $\gamma_{11} \equiv 1 \pmod\ell$, and $c \not\equiv 1 \pmod{\mathfrak{m}_W}$ whenever $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)$ and $\tau \neq \mathrm{id}$; (v) two primes of $S$ not containing both coordinate classes, both containing the class of $C(\sigma\varpi)$ and each containing a linear form $a_iX_0 + b_iX_1$ modulo $(X_0,X_1)^2$ with $q \nmid a_1b_2 - a_2b_1$, have distinct contractions along $e \circ \mathrm{toC}$; (vi) for a prime $P$ of $S$ not containing both coordinate classes, containing the class of $C(\sigma\varpi)$ and containing $X_0$ modulo $(X_0,X_1)^2$, an element $a \in C$ satisfies $\mathrm{toC}(\mathrm{germY}\,a) \in e^{-1}P$ if and only if every Laurent coefficient of $a$ lies in the image of $\mathfrak{m}_A$; (vii) [`ModularCurve.jqNModC L q`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L18) lies in $K$ and in $C$, and there are $a_0 \in A$ with $\mathrm{jqNModC} - a_0 \in y'$, an integer $e_0 \ge 1$ and $h \in (X_0,X_1)^{e_0}$ whose $e_0$-th homogeneous part takes unit values at every pair $(a,b) \in W^2$ with $a$ or $b$ a unit and $a^qb - ab^q \in \mathfrak{m}_W$, such that $e(\mathrm{toC}(\mathrm{germY}(\mathrm{jqNModC} - a_0)))$ is the class of $h$.
--
--   Now fix such a point $z$ with germ $\varpi_z$ of $\varpi$ in the maximal ideal of $\mathcal{O}_{X,z}$ (`hϖz`, `hz`), a point $y'$ of `XFin A ↥K j` over $z$ (`hy'`) satisfying the supersingularity condition `hss'`, and assume `hy'y`: the prime of $y'$ equals $y$. Fix one opened chart witness at $z$: a complete discrete valuation domain $W_1$, $\sigma_1 : A \to W_1$ with $\mathfrak{m}_{W_1} = (\sigma_1\varpi)$ (`hσ₁`), $f_1,u_1,v_1 \in W_1[[X_0,X_1]]$ with $u_1,v_1$ units and $f_1$ congruent to the Drinfeld form modulo $(X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$ (`hf₁`), and a ring isomorphism $e_1$ from the adic completion of $\mathcal{O}_{X,z}$ onto $S_1 := W_1[[X_0,X_1]]/(C(\sigma_1(\varpi_t^{q+1}))v_1 - f_1u_1)$; the hypothesis `hW₁` asserts the same seven clauses (i)–(vii) for this data $(W_1,\sigma_1,f_1,u_1,v_1,e_1)$ at $z$ and $y'$.
--
--   Let $J$ be an ideal of $C$ which, by `hJ`, is the infimum of the set of ideals of the form $\rho_\tau^{-1}\big((e_1 \circ \mathrm{toC} \circ \mathrm{germY})^{-1}(\,(\text{classes of } C(\sigma_1\varpi_t),\,X_0,\,X_1)\,)\big)$, where $\gamma$ runs over $\Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$, $\tau$ over the level automorphisms at $\gamma^{-1}$ mapping $C$ into $C$, and $\rho_\tau$ is the induced endomorphism of $C$. Let $B$ be the $A$-subalgebra of $K$ which, by `hB`, is generated over $C$ by $\{x \in K : x\varpi_t \in J\}$, and let $W$ be a valuation subring of $K$ containing $B$ (`hBW`). The hypotheses on the pair $(B,W)$ are: `hR1` — $C \le B$ and every element of $K$ is a quotient $g/h$ with $g,h \in B$, $h \neq 0$; `hR2` — $A \to B$ is formally smooth and of finite presentation and $B/(\varpi)$ has Krull dimension at most $1$; `hR3` (five clauses) — an element of $L$ lies in $W$ exactly when it comes from $A$, the maximal ideal of $W$ is generated by $\varpi$, $W$ is a discrete valuation ring, an element of $C$ lies in $y$ exactly when it lies in the maximal ideal of $W$, and $f \in K$ lies in $W$ exactly when $f = g/h$ with $g,h \in B$ and $h$ a unit of $W$; and `hEQ` (five clauses, summarised here) — for every $\mathbb{F}_{q^2}$-algebra structure on the residue field $k$ of $A$ there is a surjection $\rho : B \to$ [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q k`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21) (the quotient of $k[X_0,X_1]$ by `drinfeldPoly q k - 1`) whose kernel is the set of elements of $B$ in the maximal ideal of $W$, which is compatible with $A \to k$ and which, for each $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ and each level automorphism $\tau$ at $\gamma^{-1}$ preserving $W$, is equivariant for some $c \in \mathbb{F}_{q^2}^\times$ with $(\mathrm{redQ}\,q\,\gamma, c)$ in [`DrinfeldCurve.hSubgroup q`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L276) (the kernel of `hChar q`) acting through [`DrinfeldCurve.hAction`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L325), with $c \neq 1$ when $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)$ and $\tau \neq \mathrm{id}$; further, $B$ is stable under all such $\tau$; every prime of $B$ containing $\varpi$ is hit by the image under some such $\tau$ with $\gamma \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$ of the elements of $B$ lying in the maximal ideal of $W$; an element of $B$ whose images under all such $\tau$ lie in the maximal ideal of $W$ is divisible by $\varpi$; and $W$ is $\tau$-stable whenever $\tau$ preserves $y$ on $C$. It is also assumed that [`ModularCurve.jqNModC L q`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L18) lies in $K$ (`hjK`) and in $C$ (`hjC`).
--
--   Finally, let $m \ge 1$ with $\varpi^m = \varpi_t$ times a unit (`hm1`, `hmt`), and let $O$ be a subring of $K$ subject to the end data: `hO` provides $a' \in J \subseteq C$ with $a' \neq 0$ such that, writing $B_{a'}$ for the $A$-subalgebra generated over $C$ by $\{x \in K : xa' \in J\}$, there is a maximal ideal $P$ of $B_{a'}$ with $O$ equal to the localisation of $B_{a'}$ at $P$ inside $K$, with every element of $y$ a non-unit of $O$, and with $B \not\subseteq O$; `hOloc` and `hOnoe` make $O$ local and Noetherian; `hCO` places $C$ inside $O$ and `hOy` identifies the contraction of the maximal ideal of $O$ to $C$ with $y$. Let $\iota_1$ be a ring isomorphism from the adic completion of $O$ at its maximal ideal onto the crossing model `UVCrossingModel W₁ ((σ₁ ϖ)^m)`, that is $W_1[[X_0,X_1]]/(X_0X_1 - C((\sigma_1\varpi)^m))$, carrying constants from $A$ to the corresponding `UVCrossingModel.const` (`hι₁c`). Let $a \in C$ with $a \in J$ and $a \neq 0$, let $c \in O$, and let $\gamma_U, \gamma_V$ be units of the crossing model, subject to: `hJa`, every element of $J$ is $a$ times an element of $O$; `hac`, $a\,c = \varpi_t$ in $K$; `hιa`, $\iota_1(a) = \gamma_V \cdot V((\sigma_1\varpi)^m)$; and `hιc`, $\iota_1(c) = \gamma_U \cdot U((\sigma_1\varpi)^m)$. Lastly, `hyB` requires the ideal of $B$ generated by the image of $y$ to be prime.
--
--   The conclusion is the single assertion that every $f \in K$ lying in $O$ lies in $W$, i.e. $O \subseteq W$ as subrings of $K$.
--
--   This is a dominance statement in the local study of the supersingular fibre of the modular curve of level $\Gamma_{H_1}(q^2M')$ over the Henselian base $A$: the local ring of an end of the weighted blow-up chart $C[J/a]$, presented through a $UV$-crossing model, is contained in the exceptional valuation ring $W$ attached to the chart $B = C[J/\varpi_t]$. It is used in the construction of the ring homomorphism and tangent coordinates at such an end in the $\Gamma_1(\ell)$-diamond frame for small $q$.
